 + (-2)^{2})\\,i+(2 (-1) (-2) + 8 (-2))\\,j \\\\  & =(-8)\\,i+(-12)\\,j \\\\  & =⟨-8,-12⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the Cartesian equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(-1,-2)\\cdot ⟨x-(-1),\\,y-(-2)⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-8,-12⟩\\cdot ⟨x + 1,\\,y + 2⟩ & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521682 1080 "⟨\\frac{111}{2},-20⟩\\cdot ⟨x + \\frac{3}{2},\\,y + \\frac{5}{2}⟩=0" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521682 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521682 1083 #uuid "1d12fff6-b9f1-57fd-a747-267328625646" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521683 1080 "⟨- \\frac{111}{2},-20⟩\\cdot ⟨x - \\frac{3}{2},\\,y + \\frac{5}{2}⟩=0" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521683 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521683 1083 #uuid "1d6289d5-24ff-5c6c-97cc-fd398c028f1d" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521684 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521726 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521684 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521684 1071 "Given the function $f(x,y)=- 5 x^{2} + 5 x y^{2} + 2 y^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent line to the level curve that passes through the point where $(x,y)=(- \\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}).$" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521684 1072 #uuid "20ccc6f9-9078-5553-ae96-b36095f293ae" 13194139535597 17592186045443 true] [17592186521684 1074 "The equation of the tangent line to the level curve $f(x,y)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y)$ and evaluate it at $(x,y)=(- \\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2}):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y) & ={f}_{x}(x,y)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}